# There is exactly one environment variable in this project, and it is optional.
#
# The site is fully static: no database, no authentication, no API keys, no
# server secrets. The contact form opens a pre-filled WhatsApp message in the
# visitor's own WhatsApp session, so nothing is submitted to a backend.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL — PUBLIC, never secret.
#   Purpose:  sets the canonical URL and the absolute Open Graph URLs used for
#             link previews on WhatsApp, LinkedIn, Instagram and X.
#   Value:    your deployed origin including the scheme, e.g.
#             https://muhammed-hashir.vercel.app
#   Where:    Vercel -> Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables
#   Required? No. On Vercel the deployment hostname is detected automatically,
#             so leaving this unset still produces correct previews. Set it only
#             when you connect a custom domain, so previews point at the domain
#             you actually share.
#   Local:    leave blank. The dev server falls back to localhost and omits the
#             canonical tag rather than emitting a bogus public URL.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
